[1m[38;5;231mWhat should the logger capture?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mErrors + breadcrumbs (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mUncaught errors and rejections, plus key login-flow events (validation outcome, login attempt, API result). Enough
[39m     [38;5;246mtrail to reconstruct a failure.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Errors only
     [38;5;246mUncaught exceptions, unhandled rejections, explicit error calls. Lowest volume and cost; often leaves you unable to
[39m     [38;5;246msee what led to the error.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Verbose with level filter
     [38;5;246mLog liberally at debug/info/warn/error, ship only at or above a configurable threshold. Most flexible; risks high [39m
     [38;5;246mvolume and cost if the threshold slips.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
